% The Pit Takes One (resource scarcity: an irreversible fill)
%
% A narrow pit in the middle of a stone crossing. On the crossing squat a
% giant beetle and a drone, dripping from the sluice. Both are bulky: the
% first body that falls into the pit fills it, and after that the pit is
% only floor. Two companions, one skill each, from six.
%
%   tower --- ledge (team) --- crossing (beetle, drone; the pit) --- far
%
% The beetle is an insect: the cold kills it (blizzard), and the pit
% takes it. The drone is a soaked machine: a jolt kills it
% (lightningFlash), and the pit takes it too. The pit is the scarce thing:
% it takes only one.
%
% Methods:
%   beetle in the pit   knock it in - a fireball or a shield bash from the
%                       ledge, a wave on the crossing, a vortex on the pit
%                       (it draws both, and the beetle, nearer, lands
%                       first); then jolt the drone (lightningFlash)
%   drone in the pit    ice the crossing (blizzard): the beetle dies, the
%                       drone only freezes; then knock the drone in
%   no pit              jolt the drone, then ice the beetle (the order
%                       matters: see below)
%
% Traps:
%   - a knock or a vortex takes whichever it lands on first: with a
%     knocker and the cold, a vortex before the blizzard fills the pit
%     with the beetle, and the frozen drone is left standing;
%   - two knockers: the second body finds the pit full;
%   - ice before the jolt: the cold freezes the soaked drone (a stun), and
%     the freeze dries it - the jolt then only stuns it again;
%   - fire before the jolt: the fireball's flames fill the crossing and
%     steam the drone dry. Jolt first, then knock the beetle in.
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; 9 pairs do (18 of 36
% assignments), by methods of three kinds; the order is the puzzle.

% === Map: four areas; the pit is a feature of the crossing ===
region(ledge).
region(tower).
region(crossing).
region(far).
connected(tower, ledge).
connected(ledge, crossing).
connected(crossing, far).
lineOfSight(ledge, crossing).
lineOfSight(tower, crossing).
lineOfSight(far, crossing).

feature(crossing, pit, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, ledge).
at(mage, ledge).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).

% === Enemies: both fill the pit when they fall ===
role(beetle, enemy).
at(beetle, crossing).
tag(beetle, insect).
tag(beetle, filler).

role(drone, enemy).
at(drone, crossing).
tag(drone, machine).
tag(drone, filler).
tag(drone, wet).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, fireball).
knows(mage, lightningFlash).

% === Victory: both, in either order ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(beetle), neutralize(drone)).
win :- if(), do(neutralize(drone), neutralize(beetle)).

funBlocker(beetle).
funBlocker(drone).
funBlockerGoal(beetle, neutralize(beetle)).
funBlockerGoal(drone, neutralize(drone)).
funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from six (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(blizzard).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(5).

goals(win).
